INFO:agent.loop:\u26a1 Executing tool: 'knowledge_agent' with arguments: {"source_title": "DOJ indictment and Senate/academic findings on IRA 2016 operation", "source_url": "SRC-001; SRC-003; SRC-004; SRC-002", "text": "Evidence returned by benchmark tools: The DOJ indictment (SRC-001) alleges that the Russian organization Internet Research Agency operated from around 2014 to interfere with U.S. political processes including the 2016 presidential election; received funding from Yevgeniy Prigozhin and Concord entities; used false U.S. personas, stolen identities, U.S.-facing social-media pages/groups, U.S. servers, staged rallies, paid ads, and unwitting U.S. persons. It identifies a strategic goal of sowing discord, and says by early-to-mid 2016 operations supported Donald Trump and disparaged Hillary Clinton. The indictment describes hundreds of employees, a millions-of-dollars annual budget, a translator project operating on YouTube, Facebook, Instagram, and Twitter, a stated goal of spreading distrust toward candidates and the political system, and Project Lakhta funding exceeding 73 million rubles/month (over $1.25m) in September 2016, with funds routed through affiliates and disguised as software support. It names Concord as primary funder and Prigozhin as controller of Concord. The Senate report (SRC-003) states that IRA operatives masqueraded as Americans, used targeted ads, falsified news, self-generated content and platform tools to reach/attempt to deceive tens of millions; sought polarization over societal, ideological and racial differences; and found the IRA sought to harm Clinton and support Trump at Kremlin direction. It says the campaign was broader than the election, emphasizing race, immigration, guns, anger, outrage, protest and distrust in government; African-Americans were the most targeted group. It reports Blacktivist generated 11.2m Facebook engagements; over 66% of Facebook ad content contained a race-related term; 96% of YouTube content targeted racial issues/police brutality; nearly 3,400 Facebook/Instagram ads, 61,500 Facebook posts, 116,000 Instagram posts, and 10.4m tweets. It says ads were not the main activity, with about $100,000 ad spend over two years versus approximately $1.25m/month operational costs, and that the IRA coopted unwitting Americans for petitions, personal information, self-defense courses, and rallies. The academic report (SRC-004) says campaigns reached tens of millions, over 30m users shared Facebook/Instagram posts from 2015-17, activity began on Twitter in 2013 and evolved into Facebook, Instagram and YouTube, and tactics included urging African-American voters to boycott elections or use wrong voting procedures, encouraging extreme right-wing confrontation, and spreading sensationalist/conspiratorial/junk political news. NPR (SRC-002) summarizes Senate findings: African Americans were singled out; Blacktivist had 11.2m engagements; post-election activity increased on Instagram 238%, Facebook 59%, Twitter 52%, and YouTube citations 84%; activity was overtly/almost invariably pro-Trump and anti-Clinton, at Kremlin direction."}
